{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1072","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1072","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1072\",\"parent_revision\":\"db51c03d14f4e48c13008dfdb79a01b698020802\",\"root_revision\":\"0576e61ddd417ff436f5266e3fb4994565c2faca7838b6c3b1e7716bdf3fae89\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nReplace `dict[str, Any]` return type on `_graphql_request` with per-operation Pydantic (or TypedDict) response models. Currently all 10+ GraphQL queries/mutations return untyped `dict[str, Any]`, losing type safety at every call site.\\n\\nDefine response models for each operation (IssueResponse, MilestoneResponse, CommentResponse, SearchResponse, etc.) so callers receive strongly-typed objects and `.get()` chains become attribute access.\\n\\nApproach: keep `_graphql_request` generic (TypeVar bound to BaseModel), have each public function declare its own return type via a `response_model: type[T]` argument, parse the top-level response, and return the typed result.\\n\\nCurrent state: `dict[str, Any]` was adopted in fix(backlog-core) as a pragmatic unblock for ty 0.0.25 errors. This item tracks the proper typing work.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `_graphql_request` in github.py returns `dict[str, Any]` | AVAILABLE | Item description confirms this |\\n| 2 | Number of GraphQL operations to model (10+) | AVAILABLE | Item description states '10+ queries/mutations' |\\n| 3 | Each operation's response shape | DERIVABLE | Inspect actual GraphQL query strings in github.py |\\n| 4 | TypeVar generic pattern for _graphql_request | AVAILABLE | Standard Python generics |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information available or derivable.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **pydantic response models for github graphql operations in backlog_core** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: ty 0.0.25 upgrade session 2026-03-25 \u2014 _graphql_request type fix required Any as pragmatic unblock\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Refactor. Medium complexity. Typing improvement with zero behavioral change. Risk: response shape assumptions must match actual GitHub API responses.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Response models defined for every GraphQL operation in `github.py`: `IssueResponse`, `MilestoneResponse`, `CommentResponse`, `SearchResponse`, and others as needed\\n- `_graphql_request` becomes generic: `TypeVar T` bound to `BaseModel`; accepts `response_model: type[T]` argument; returns `T`\\n- All call sites updated to receive typed objects (attribute access replaces `.get()` chains)\\n- `ty check` and `ruff check` pass with zero new suppressions introduced\\n- No `dict[str, Any]` remains in the GraphQL response handling path\\n- Regression: all existing backlog_core tests pass\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 define response models, update `_graphql_request`, update all callers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 update tests that expect `dict[str, Any]` return types\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a type checker running against backlog_core, I need `_graphql_request` and all GitHub GraphQL callers to use per-operation Pydantic/TypedDict response models instead of `dict[str, Any]` so call sites have strong typing and `.get()` chains become typed attribute access.\\n\",\"digest\":\"87c338cfaa0f683d6968ca533d5b53ee407c11ca3b340d372808a6604c6b5feb\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg6bvA\"}"}